### Page 1 of 3

```text
February 18, 2014
Quick Overview of Specification Updates
Section 01000 – General Use of Specifications – New section with information concerning their use and
how they are implemented, updated and reviewed.
Section 01041 – Project Coordination – Update requires one ROW permit to be pulled on the project.
Clarifies what drawings are required to be submitted with ROW permit. Clarifies “emergency work”: and
when permits are due to be turned in.  Takes out the dollar amount for BOPU inspection fees and directs
contractor to call BOPU for current price.
Section 01050 Traffic Control – Clarifies Traffic Engineering Dept. for approvals and acceptance of
certain items.
Section 01054 – Control of Work  - clarifies acceptance, warranty work time frames and as-builts.
Introduces and requires infrastructure asset sheets.
Section 01231 - Safety – Outlines requirements for pedestrian paths through construction areas.
Section 01505 – Temporary Facilities – a little more detail for Job trailers and sanitation facilities.
Section 01562 – Dust Control and Clean Up – A little more teeth in dust and mud control and spelled
out when inspections are called for, the area to be inspected must be free of mud, snow ice, ect.
Section 01563 – Erosion Control and Storm Water Management – complete rewrite done a couple
years ago. Addressed BMP materials. Requires sediment bag for pumping unless a settling pond is
utilized, requires water tight concrete wash out.
Section 02051 - Abandoned Pipe Systems – New Section - Found a need to have a specification on pipes
being abandoned in the ROW. Includes pipe plugs, manhole and water valve abandonment. Also calls for
all pipe left in ground to be “Flash Filled”.
Section 02075 – Demolition of Asphalt and Portland Cement Concrete – Corrects the method of
measurement and basis of payment.  Other minor cleanup.
Section 02076 – Cold Milling Existing Pavement – New Section – The City has been using a version of
this specification as a supplemental in its paving projects for many years.  It was decided to make it a
standard specification as it has started to be needed on development projects as well.
Section 2190 – Aggregates – Increases fractured faces from 85% to 95% having one or more fractured
faces and increases fractured faces from 80% to 90% having two or more in flexible pavements. Granite
for Plant Mix Pavements required on collectors and arterials.
Section 02205 – Directional Boring – includes requirements to show all utilities within 15 feet of
proposed bore path. Gives separation requirements from sewer and water mains as well as fire
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
hydrants. Needs to include vertical separation requirements too. Basis of payment has been added to
the specification as well.
Section 02206 – Potholing -New Section  - Locate requirements and when and where they need to
pothole in relation to the type of work they are doing. Backfill and surface restoration requirements.
Section 02210 – Excavation, Embankment and Compaction – requires a blue top be placed within two
feet of manholes to verify structure will not require over 6” of adjusting rings after paving.
Section 02225 – Trench Backfill – Requires approval in writing when bedding materials do not meet
standard specifications. Clarifies tests represent 100 foot of trench backfill, 50 foot each side of failing
compaction tests. Changes verbiage for consolidating, not compacting pea gravel. Removes compaction
testing of bedding materials. Again, blue tops within 2 foot of manholes to check for adjustment rings.
Section 02226 – Backfilling for Appurtenances – Requires additional compaction testing around
structures and over pipes. Tells contractor that any settlement around appurtenances shall be their
responsibility for the two year warranty period.
Section 02227 – Alley and Gravel Street Restoration – New section. – Casper specification for alley and
gravel street restoration. – requires 6” of material be placed. Material -  100 % passes a 11/2” sieve and
90% retained on a ¾” sieve. Reduces sediment from alleys.
Section 02512 – Plant Mix Pavements – Reduces requirement for a new mix design each year and only
requires mix verification testing by an independent lab each year. Gives wide band limits for JMF
aggregates verification. Requires a gradation and asphalt binder content be submitted each day.
Requires a moisture content minimum during production to be tested once per day when supplying for
City roads. Includes addition of lime requirements during production which was inadvertently left out in
the last rewrite.
02515 Asphalt Patching – Requires a minimum of 6” patch on all roads classified higher than local.
Requires tack be placed on concrete surfaces abutting asphalt. “T” patches required, parallel and
perpendicular to traffic patch, no patches in wheel paths.
Section 02570 – Adjusting Street Fixtures – clarifies that no payment be made to adjust “new” street
fixtures to grade.
Section 02645 – Fire Hydrant Assembly -  requires plastic to be placed over drain rock for separation
from backfill materials. Clarifies what payment covers.
Section 02665 – Water Distribution and Transmission Systems – Adds reference AWWA-116/A21.16-
09. Requires epoxy coated exteriors and interiors on fittings. Calls out Star Grip Megalugs as being
approved for certain pipe, valve box and adapters acceptable, corp stops call outs, meter pit
requirement changes. Increases tap size contractors can self perform. Various other small material
changes.
```

### Page 3 of 3

```text
Section 02667 – Cold Water Meters – One small material call out changed.
Section 02675 Disinfection – calls out new approved adhesive for tablets.
Section 02700 Sanitary Sewer Systems – requires all material be two years old or less. Changes from
DFW non shear couplings to Mission Flex Seal sewer repair couplings.
Section 02725 Storm Drains and Culverts – Changes requirements for flared end, head walls sections.
Video inspection and deflection testing with mandrel after 30 days. Changed payment method called
out for manholes, cleaned up payment items.
Section 02805 – Installation, Relocation or Replacement of street Signs, Utility Posts and Mail Boxes –
Change to post design, pole inbedment, pole lengths contractor responsible for, post measurement
changes.
Section 02806 – Size, Fabrication Material and design of New Traffic Signs – changes as requested by
Mark – Font size changes and other clean up. Clarifies Traffic Engineering Dept. approves submittals.
Section 03304 – Portland Cement Concrete – just a little verbiage to clean up a couple dubious
statements.
Section 03310 – Concrete Work – Changed number to call for inspections to permit office rather than
our secretaries.  Calls out when honeycombed concrete will be pulled.
Section 03330 – Concrete Curbs and Combined Curbs and Gutters – Quantifies testing requirements for
R&R vs new.
Section 03340 – Concrete Sidewalks, Driveway Approaches, Curb Turn Fillets, valley Gutters, and
miscellaneous New Concrete Construction – Detectable warning plates called out, testing requirements
new vs R&R. Method of Measurement – gives equation to measure fillets.
Section 03480 – Precast Concrete Units – Quality assurance updated, NPCA and ACPA requirements.
Section 03600 – Grout – Changes requirements for Portland Cement Grout from a prescriptive
specification to a more performance based specification.
```
